{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Let the [G]rocks cry [C]out. Let the [G]people [C]shout,
For the [Em]King has [D]come [Dsus]to [G]claim His [C]throne.
For the [G]Son who [C]lives is the [G]one who [C]gives
His [Em]life to [D]save [Dsus]my [G]wretched [C]soul.
Halle[Em]lujah, [G]Lord of all!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]At your [D]feet we [C]bow.
[G]On our [D]knees we fall [C]down.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Let Your [G]praises [C]ring, ever [G]echo[C]ing,
For Your [Em7]blood has [D]bought [Dsus]me [G]liber[C]ty.
Let Your [G]church pro[C]claim Your e[G]ternal [C]name
For the [Em7]Son of [D]God [Dsus]has [G]overcome the grave.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
[G]At your [D]feet we [C]bow.
[G]On our [D]knees we fall [C]down.
[G]At your [D]feet we [C]bow.
[G]On our [D]knees we fall [C]down.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Em7]You [D/F#]are the [G]love that gives [C]everything.
[Em7]You [D/F#]are the [G]author of [C]history.
[Em7]You [D/F#]are the [G]refuge [Am]that I [D]need.
[Em]You [D/F#]are the [G]righteous and [C]worthy.
[Em]You [D/F#]are the [G]steadfast be[C]fore me.
[Em]All [D/F#]hail the [G]name a[Am]bove all [D]names!
{end_of_bridge}
